From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] host_shaders: bounds-check the ASTC decode and every unswizzle store

Ported from Frizti/Fritchii commit f52631cf6, shipped in Fritchii v5.2, which describes it as "AMD:
textures no longer write into other textures' memory. Images whose size isn't a multiple of their
block size wrote past their edge while being decoded. NVIDIA ignores that, AMD put it in other
textures: black blocks, a crosshatch, and in the end a GPU crash."

That is this device's situation exactly. The PS5 runs RADV on RDNA2, and the commit's own comment
names an RX 6750 XT - the same family - for the symptom: a block at the right or bottom edge of an
image whose size is not a multiple of the block size stored texels past it, which on AMD landed in
other images' memory and eventually faulted the GPU on an invalid write. NVIDIA dropped them.

The fix is a guard at every store site:

- astc_decoder.comp keeps the destination's extent in image_extent and routes all three imageStore
  calls (FillError, FillVoidExtentLDR, DecompressBlock) through StoreTexel, which drops a texel
  outside it.
- block_linear_unswizzle_2d.comp, block_linear_unswizzle_3d.comp and pitch_unswizzle.comp return
  before their imageStore when the coordinate is outside the image, because their workgroups round
  the dispatch up past the edge.

What this can break: a texel that would have been written is now skipped, so an edge block whose
decode relied on the overrun shows a partial block where it used to show whatever memory it ran
into. That is the intended trade - the overrun was undefined, and on this hardware it landed in other
images. The cost is one vector compare and a branch per stored texel in four small compute shaders.

Measured or a guess: the symptom, the hardware family and the GPU fault are upstream's, measured on
an RX 6750 XT. Whether it is one of the defects in our own screenshots is not established - our log
carries no crosshatch or black-block report under that name, and no console has run this build. It is
included because it is a verified AMD corruption and device-loss bug on the GPU family this port
targets, at almost no cost.

diff --git a/src/video_core/host_shaders/astc_decoder.comp b/src/video_core/host_shaders/astc_decoder.comp
index 01bec11f1..6e7dd2d93 100644
--- a/src/video_core/host_shaders/astc_decoder.comp
+++ b/src/video_core/host_shaders/astc_decoder.comp
@@ -1095,10 +1095,22 @@ int FindLayout(uint mode) {
 }
 
 
+// The image's size: a block at the right or bottom edge of an image whose size isn't a multiple
+// of the block size reaches past it. Storing those texels anyway is undefined; on AMD they landed
+// in other images' memory (black blocks and a crosshatch in Ocarina of Time on an RX 6750 XT, and
+// at last a GPU fault on an invalid write), where NVIDIA dropped them.
+ivec3 image_extent;
+
+void StoreTexel(ivec3 texel, vec4 value) {
+    if (all(lessThan(texel.xy, image_extent.xy))) {
+        imageStore(dest_image, texel, value);
+    }
+}
+
 void FillError(ivec3 coord) {
     for (uint j = 0; j < block_dims.y; j++) {
         for (uint i = 0; i < block_dims.x; i++) {
-            imageStore(dest_image, coord + ivec3(i, j, 0), vec4(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0));
+            StoreTexel(coord + ivec3(i, j, 0), vec4(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0));
         }
     }
 }
@@ -1115,7 +1127,7 @@ void FillVoidExtentLDR(ivec3 coord) {
     const float b = float(b_u) / 65535.0f;
     for (uint j = 0; j < block_dims.y; j++) {
         for (uint i = 0; i < block_dims.x; i++) {
-            imageStore(dest_image, coord + ivec3(i, j, 0), vec4(r, g, b, a));
+            StoreTexel(coord + ivec3(i, j, 0), vec4(r, g, b, a));
         }
     }
 }
@@ -1389,7 +1401,7 @@ void DecompressBlock(ivec3 coord) {
                 p = Cf / 65535.0f;
             }
 
-            imageStore(dest_image, coord + ivec3(i, j, 0), clamp(p, 0.0f, 1.0f).gbar);
+            StoreTexel(coord + ivec3(i, j, 0), clamp(p, 0.0f, 1.0f).gbar);
         }
     }
 }
@@ -1421,7 +1433,8 @@ void main() {
     offset += swizzle;
 
     const ivec3 coord = ivec3(gl_GlobalInvocationID * uvec3(block_dims, 1));
-    if (any(greaterThanEqual(coord, imageSize(dest_image)))) {
+    image_extent = imageSize(dest_image);
+    if (any(greaterThanEqual(coord, image_extent))) {
         return;
     }
     local_buff = astc_data[offset / 16];
diff --git a/src/video_core/host_shaders/block_linear_unswizzle_2d.comp b/src/video_core/host_shaders/block_linear_unswizzle_2d.comp
index bbe73acd1..5f2d11d18 100644
--- a/src/video_core/host_shaders/block_linear_unswizzle_2d.comp
+++ b/src/video_core/host_shaders/block_linear_unswizzle_2d.comp
@@ -127,5 +127,10 @@ void main() {
 
     const uvec4 texel = ReadTexel(offset);
     const ivec3 coord = ivec3(gl_GlobalInvocationID) + destination;
+    // Workgroups round the dispatch up past the image; on AMD a store outside it lands in other
+    // memory (see astc_decoder.comp).
+    if (any(greaterThanEqual(coord, imageSize(output_image)))) {
+        return;
+    }
     imageStore(output_image, coord, texel);
 }
diff --git a/src/video_core/host_shaders/block_linear_unswizzle_3d.comp b/src/video_core/host_shaders/block_linear_unswizzle_3d.comp
index 8dfaf0cd1..9df13369c 100644
--- a/src/video_core/host_shaders/block_linear_unswizzle_3d.comp
+++ b/src/video_core/host_shaders/block_linear_unswizzle_3d.comp
@@ -130,5 +130,10 @@ void main() {
 
     const uvec4 texel = ReadTexel(offset);
     const ivec3 coord = ivec3(gl_GlobalInvocationID) + destination;
+    // Workgroups round the dispatch up past the image; on AMD a store outside it lands in other
+    // memory (see astc_decoder.comp).
+    if (any(greaterThanEqual(coord, imageSize(output_image)))) {
+        return;
+    }
     imageStore(output_image, coord, texel);
 }
diff --git a/src/video_core/host_shaders/pitch_unswizzle.comp b/src/video_core/host_shaders/pitch_unswizzle.comp
index 7d23f594c..49196f21e 100644
--- a/src/video_core/host_shaders/pitch_unswizzle.comp
+++ b/src/video_core/host_shaders/pitch_unswizzle.comp
@@ -81,5 +81,10 @@ void main() {
 
     const uvec4 texel = ReadTexel(offset);
     const ivec2 coord = ivec2(gl_GlobalInvocationID.xy) + destination;
+    // Workgroups round the dispatch up past the image; on AMD a store outside it lands in other
+    // memory (see astc_decoder.comp).
+    if (any(greaterThanEqual(coord, imageSize(output_image)))) {
+        return;
+    }
     imageStore(output_image, coord, texel);
 }
